module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.FpqcHomSheafRefinement
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.PullbackSectionsSheaf.HomPresheaf
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Topologies.SiteStructureSheaf

/-!
# Sheaves on a site of schemes over a base whose coverings are fpqc coverings

Let `S` be a scheme and let a site of schemes over `S` be given by a precoverage `K` on a
category `C` together with a functor `toOver : C ⥤ Over S`.  If every covering family of `K`
becomes an fpqc covering family of schemes, then the presheaf of global functions `𝒪` of the
site is a sheaf of rings, and for every quasi-coherent module `F` on `S` the presheaf
`(f : T ⟶ S) ↦ Γ(T, f^*F)` is a sheaf on the site, so that the associated module `Fᵃ` is a
sheaf of `𝒪`-modules there.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Sites.fpqcSiteStructureSheaf` is the structure sheaf of rings of such a site.
* `Stacks.Sites.fpqcSiteAssociatedModule` is `Fᵃ` as a sheaf of `𝒪`-modules on such a site.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_type_op_comp_of_precoverage`: the restriction of a sheaf of types along
  a compatible-preserving functor is a sheaf for a topology generated by a precoverage whose
  generating families have covering images.
* `Stacks.Sites.compatiblePreserving_toOver`: the canonical functor to the schemes over `S` is
  compatible-preserving for the fpqc topology induced on `Over S`.
* `Stacks.Sites.coverPreserving_toScheme_of_mem_fpqcPrecoverage` and
  `Stacks.Sites.functorPushforward_toOver_mem_fpqcOver`: a site whose covering families become
  fpqc covering families of schemes has covering images in the schemes over `S`.
* `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_structurePresheaf_of_mem_fpqcPrecoverage`: **the presheaf `𝒪` is a sheaf
  on such a site.**
* `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_associatedPresheaf_of_mem_fpqcPrecoverage`: the presheaf of pullback
  sections of a quasi-coherent module on `S` is a sheaf on such a site.
* `Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_presheafHom_toOver_of_mem_fpqcPrecoverage`: the presheaf of *morphisms*
  of the pullbacks of two quasi-coherent modules on `S` is a sheaf on such a site.

## Implementation notes

The site is presented by a precoverage `K` with `CategoryTheory.Precoverage.HasPullbacks` and
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.IsStableUnderBaseChange`, together with fibre products of `C` that
the canonical functor to all schemes preserves.  That is the site axioms of the source for a
full subcategory of the schemes over `S`: a covering may be based-changed along any morphism,
and the fibre products used for it are the fibre products of schemes.

The sheaf assertions here assume that `C` has all fibre products and that they are fibre products
of schemes.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03OJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03OJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03OG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03OG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DT)
